# Model artifacts, regenerated by `python train.py`.
#
# The training bundle (model_bundle.joblib, metrics.json, manifest.json) is a
# joblib pickle whose contents are bound to exact library versions, so tracking
# it would recreate exactly the class of problem Issue #4/#2 documented: a
# model artifact in the repo that silently disagrees with the code that
# produced it. A fresh clone plus `python train.py` rebuilds it bit-for-bit.
#
# EXCEPTION -- artifacts/production/ IS tracked. That four-file set is the
# serving contract (app.py reads nothing else), it is what makes a fresh clone
# run the app out-of-the-box, and its integrity is machine-checked: metadata.json
# records the sha256 of the three sibling files, and `python
# export_production.py --verify-only` re-checks them plus the forest/scaler/
# calibration content fingerprints. It is regenerated deterministically by
# `python train.py && python export_production.py`.
#
# Note: `artifacts/*` (not `artifacts/`) is required here -- git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/production/
artifacts_*/

# Streamlit
.streamlit/

